From 5c458867def82134757ef415595816c8e8b137da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 01:36:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op camera: the module may turn the player camera's yaw and
 pitch

The co-op module's Customize page turns the camera around the player's
own Link. Through hos_coop_view (patch 0019) it can only replace the eye
and target after the camera has placed itself, so the game's collision
never saw the module's eye: next to a cliff the eye went inside the rock.

A new optional export, hos_coop_turn (host/hos_coop_turn.h), is asked
by hos_mouse_camera at the start of each update of the player camera
(f_80644c80), before the Mouse camera row's check. It gets the camera's
yaw (+0x1a4), pitch (+0x18c) and state (+0x204) and may hand back new
angles. They are written only in states 3 and 4 (the camera follows Link
or the player turns it), the yaw wrapped into -180..180 and the pitch
kept in the camera's limits (+0x178). The camera's update then runs as
always, with its own collision. While the module turns the camera, the
native mouse does not, and its angles start from the camera's again.

The bridge (host/coop_bridge.c) finds the export as the other optional
ones. A module without it: the game's camera, as before.

The camera's update does not run every frame: the game's node walker
(f_800e98c0) skips a node's update while bit 2 of its byte +31 is set,
and left idle the player camera's stops for seconds, so the Customize
page got no call. hos_mouse_camera remembers the last camera it ran for;
the view hook asks the module (hos_coop_turn with no angles, state -1)
whether it wants the camera, and while it does and the update has not
run for 50 ms, hos_coop_camera_wake clears that bit on the game's thread.
The node's flag words are logged once per new pair (at most 16).
